            "plain": "<p>As a <strong>tile-laying artist</strong>, you have been <strong>challenged to embellish the walls of the Royal Palace of \u00c9vora </strong>in Portugal.<br></p>\n<p>In the game Azul, take turns <strong>drafting colored tiles</strong> from suppliers to your player board. Score your points based on how you've placed your tiles to decorate the palace.</p>\n<p>Extra points are scored for <strong>specific patterns and completing sets</strong>. But be strategic\u2013 wasted supplies will harm your score.</p>\n<p>Receive the most points for your decoration and win the game!</p>\n<p>Check out all of the <a href=\"https://twentysidedstore.com/search?q=azul*&amp;type=product\" title=\"Azul Games and Expansions\" target=\"_blank\">Azul games and expansions</a>!</p>\n<h3>Contents</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>100 Resin Tiles</li>\n<li>4 Player Boards</li>\n<li>9 Factory Displays</li>\n<li>4 Scoring Markers</li>\n<li>1 Starting Player Marker</li>\n<li>1 Linen Bag</li>\n<li>1 Rulebook</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Details</h3>\nPlayers: 2 - 4<br>Ages: 8+<br>Runtime: 30 - 45m<br>Designer: Michael Kiesling"
